! eco-COBALT parameter overrides. Intentionally empty: the branch defaults are
! the tested configuration, and COBALT_parameter_doc.all after a run is the
! authoritative list of what was actually used.
!
! All ~340 new eco-COBALT parameters are read with
!   get_param(param_file, "generic_COBALT", ...)
! i.e. from COBALT_input / COBALT_override -- NOT from the field_table, and not
! from a namelist. namelist /generic_COBALT_nml/ is unchanged by the merge, so
! input.nml needs no eco-specific edits either.
!
! Defaults worth knowing (generic_COBALT.F90 on feature/gz-cobalt-merge):
!
!   does_dvm_vmmdz = does_dvm_vmlgz = does_dvm_lgt = .true.
!   does_dvm_smz   = does_dvm_mdz   = does_dvm_lgz = does_dvm_smt = .false.
!     A FATAL check rejects does_dvm for any group other than VMMDZ/VMLGZ/LGT,
!     since only those own gut and metabolite tracers.
!
!   Switching a migrator off is supported, and takes TWO parameters.
!     does_dvm_<group> = False on its own does NOT hold a group still: it is
!     still assigned a swimming speed, and nvmmdz / nvmlgz / nlgt are registered
!     move_vertical = .true., so for those three that speed still moves the
!     biomass tracer -- the group keeps migrating, just without carrying its gut
!     and metabolite pools. Always set swim_max_<group> = 0.0 alongside;
!     generic_COBALT enforces the pairing with a FATAL.
!     See README.md, "Switching groups off".
!
!   swim_max_vmmdz / _vmlgz / _lgt = 0.06 / 0.08 / 0.04 m s-1  (0.0 elsewhere)
!   imax_vmmdz / _vmlgz / _smt / _lgt = 0.57 / 0.23 / 1.875 / 0.55 d-1 at 0 C
!   k_clear_gut_* = 8.0 d-1, k_temp_gut_* = 4.32 d-1 degC-1, k_clear_met_* = 1.0 d-1
!     (k_clear_gut_lgt / k_temp_gut_lgt are copepod values inherited by salps
!      as a starting point -- salp gut passage differs, so these are worth retuning)
!   agg_lgt = 0.082e+6 d-1 (mol N kg-1)-1 ; frac_fast_det_lgt = 0.75 ; 0.0 elsewhere
!   assim_eff_max / _min = 0.8 / 0.25 for BOTH tunicates, kae_smt = 1.34e-6 and
!     kae_lgt = 2.63e-6 mol N kg-1 -- SMT and LGT both have food-dependent AE,
!     differing only in the half-saturation. The five crustacean groups are
!     fixed at 0.7 (max = min, kae = 1.0e+10).
!   do_fastsinking = .false., wsink_fast = 1000 m/day
!     -- so fedet_fast is carried but inert in this configuration.
